Track 1: The Locomotive Bleaches the Low Drift
- Story & Context: When the primary ore hoist snapped at Shaft 11, stranding seventy workers in forty-six-degree rock heat, drill-sergeant Jano Vlok grabbed a brass wrench and began battering the high-pressure cooling duct in a frantic 13/8 mambo time signature. Rather than panicking in the dark, three trapped brass players dragged their dented horns onto the idling diesel transport and unleashed a dazzling fanfare that shook the loose shale from the tunnel arches. The vibration cleared the air valves with a deafening whistle of released steam, creating a blinding cloud that smelled of rusted iron and sulfur as the crew sang in pure, unhinged jubilation: "Strike the duct till the tunnel smells like pineapples!"
