Track 2: Who Cancelled the Noon Ore-Express?
- Story & Context: Deep inside the Level 18 Dispatch Depot, logistics clerk Mariana Cruz willfully altered thirty electronic track switches to hold the heavy ore trains in place, simply to allow the brass section to finish a twenty-minute, sunny contrapuntal fugue through the acoustic exhaust tunnels. Mariana poured sweet guava syrup into the cooling radiator fluid, filling the sweltering rail chamber with a syrupy, tropical perfume while the percussionists hammered an impossibly fast soca breakdown across the air lines. When the surface director screamed over the radio about ruined mining schedules, she laughed into the microphone and broadcast the duct-shaking wall of horns straight up to the surface office: "Tell the foreman my heart only runs on a summer schedule!"
